message.content:
Etripamil (Cardamyst) is a nasal spray, a verapamil-like phenylalkylamine derivative. It is sold as a medicament in measured doses for retail sale, so heading 3004 applies. Because it is a synthetic organic compound with no antibiotic, hormone, or alkaloid content, it falls under 3004.90. The 3004.90 subheadings include 3004.90.92 for "other" and 3004.90.91 for certain others, and the statistical suffix 3004.90.9290 is the commonly used catch-all.

The ingredient itself is a different case. Bulk etripamil would go in 2926 or 2930, but the description describes an indication, which points to the finished medicament.

{"hts_code": "3004.90.9290", "reason": "Etripamil is a finished medicament with a therapeutic indication (PSVT conversion), put up in measured doses, so it falls under heading 3004 as an 'other' medicament in 3004.90.92."}
